---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AnswerFacts from '../components/AnswerFacts.astro';
import HelpNow from '../components/HelpNow.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
const office = loadDir('resources').find((e) => e.slug === 'monongalia-county-dohs-office');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
export const page = { door: "this-month", topic: "food", label: "Apply for SNAP (food stamps)", summary: "Apply online at WV PATH, or call DoHS" };
---
<Base help title="How to apply for SNAP (food stamps) in Monongalia County, WV" description="Apply for SNAP food help online at WV PATH, the state's free site, or call DoHS customer service. Steps, phone number and sources for Morgantown and Mon County.">
  <h1>How do I apply for SNAP (food stamps) in Mon County?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Apply online at WV PATH, the state's own site. It is free. The steps are below, with the number to call the state Department of Human Services (DoHS) if you have questions.</p>

  <AnswerFacts slug="apply-for-snap-wv-path" linkLabel="Apply at WV PATH" />

  <h2>Work rules for some adults</h2>
  <p>Since November 1, 2025, some adults ages 18 through 64 must meet SNAP work rules to keep getting SNAP. Caring for a child under 14 is one of the reasons a person may not have to. DoHS decides who must meet the rules. For questions, call DoHS at <a href="tel:18777161212">1-877-716-1212</a>. <span class="meta">Source: <a href="https://dohs.wv.gov/article/west-virginia-announces-changes-snap-able-bodied-adults-without-dependents-abawd-policy">West Virginia DoHS</a>, checked October 31, 2026.</span></p>

  <h2>Rather apply in person?</h2>
  {office && <ResourceCard r={office} />}

  <p>SNAP can also buy seeds and plants that grow food. See <a href={`${base}/grow/#budget`}>Grow food on a budget</a>.</p>

  <p>Already applied? See <a href={`${base}/after-you-apply/snap/`}>what happens after you apply for SNAP</a>: the interview, letters, deadlines and how to appeal.</p>

  <HelpNow />

  <p class="meta">We describe how to apply. The state decides who gets SNAP. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
